to: review
reason: code-review-before-push
refs:
  - ta-anchor-refactor-v2/ (worktree)
  - planning/ta-anchor-refactor-v2-plan.md
  - planning/ta-anchor-refactor-review.md
note: |
  Incremental review of the third coded commit (C4-C5 still WIP; NOT push-ready).
  Base a2f49ccf (goldens tip); C1 6cea41f2, C2 4b820281 already reviewed.
  Commit:
    63a01e27 — C3 (§7) repoint the dispatch switch's queueing-model case from
      optimizeQueueingModel to a new refuseQueueingModel (log-only, no decisions);
      unconditional applySaturationDecisions then holds each model at last-good
      replicas and still emits the scaling metric. Tests 4 + 5.

  Deferral (DEFERRED, not deprecated): optimizeQueueingModel +
  runQueueingModelAnalysis + buildQMConfig are RETAINED in-tree, no longer
  dispatched. Design intent (a queueing-model-driven first-class voting analyzer)
  is preserved; re-enable by restoring the dispatch to optimizeQueueingModel. A
  blank reference (var _ = (*Engine).optimizeQueueingModel) keeps the parked
  subtree reachable so the unused linter (staticcheck U1000) does not flag it.
  The formal DEFERRED classification for the planner will also ride the eventual
  push-ready sync handoff.

  Latitude worth a reviewer eye:
    - refuseQueueingModel returns nothing (unparam would flag an always-empty
      return); it logs an error via errors.New (perfsprint wants errors.New, not
      a verbless fmt.Errorf) and leaves allDecisions empty at the call site.
    - QM ballot entry in optimizeQueueingModel sets Enabled:true + Live:true
      statically (single-analyzer path, not a per-analyzer-liveness participant) —
      unchanged behavior of the parked path, kept only for the liveness regression
      guard, since the path is no longer reached.

  Test placement:
    - Test 4A: bindingAnchor nil-condition units appended to the existing
      Describe("bindingAnchor") in pipeline/analyzer_helpers_test.go (empty ballot,
      no enabled+live+informative analyzer, ambiguous multi-binder).
    - Test 4B: new pipeline/optimizer_hold_test.go — both optimizers produce no
      decision and never index into an unbindable ballot (empty-ballot regression).
    - Test 5: new envtest It in saturation/engine_test.go piggybacking the existing
      multi-VA fixture — QM ConfigMap present routes to refuse; asserts the refusal
      is logged AND mockPromAPI.QueryCallCounts stays empty (proof of no V2/V1
      fall-through, since refuse never calls prepareModelData).

  Known coverage gap (documented, intentional): Test 5 does not assert the exact
  desiredReplicas gauge VALUE emitted by the hold path — that gauge is
  package-private and fragile to read cross-package under parallel Ginkgo. The
  refuse->hold->emit path is exercised end-to-end via optimize() returning nil
  error with the routing proof above; the hold's replica arithmetic is covered by
  the existing applySaturationDecisions tests.

  Gates green as of C3: gofmt (dirs), go build ./..., go test -count=1
  pipeline+saturation (307/307 + 98/98 specs, no pending/skipped), make lint
  (0 issues). Ship gate: #1513 goldens (optimizer_characterization_test.go) green
  after C3.
